  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)} & =\\frac{A}{(x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(2-x)}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+21x+41=A(2-x)(x+3)+B(x+1)(x+3)+C(x+1)(2-x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+21(-1)+41 & =A(2-(-1))(-1+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(-1+1)(-1+3) \\\\  & +C(-1+1)(2-(-1)) \\\\ -2-21+41 & =A(6) \\\\ A & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(2)^{2}+21(2)+41 & =A(2-2)(2+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(2+1)(2+3) \\\\  & +C(2+1)(2-2) \\\\ -8+42+41 & =B(15) \\\\ B & =\\frac{75}{15} \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-3)^{2}+21(-3)+41 & =A(2-(-3))(-3+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(-3+1)(-3+3) \\\\  & +C(-3+1)(2-(-3)) \\\\ -18-63+41 & =C(-10) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-40}{-10} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)}=\\frac{3}{(x+1)}+\\frac{5}{(2-x)}+\\frac{4}{(x+3)}.\n$$",
